     "value": "Probable component of the Arp2/3 complex in which it may replace ARPC1B (Probable). In addition to its role in the cytoplasmic cytoskeleton, the Arp2/3 complex also promotes actin polymerization in the nucleus, thereby regulating gene transcription and repair of damaged DNA (By similarity)"
